{#
  T-3.08 — the footer.

  EVERY LINK COMES FROM THE STORE MENU, AND THAT IS WHAT CLOSES OP-2. The
  register recorded an open question: the artboard's «روابط مهمة» column lists
  «المدونة» as a destination, but the blog was ruled out as the Stories source on
  2026-08-06, and three readings were possible. Building the column from
  `salla-menu source="footer"` **makes the question moot rather than answering
  it** — whether «المدونة» appears is the merchant's own footer menu in the Salla
  dashboard, and the theme neither adds the link nor removes it. Nothing here
  references `blog_link`, which was reading 2's requirement, and the link renders
  when the merchant wants it, which was reading 1's. See /docs/DERIVED-DECISIONS.md.

  WHAT THE DESIGN OMITS AND THIS TEMPLATE DROPS: upstream's `salla-apps-icons`
  and `salla-contacts` blocks. The artboard draws neither, and unlike the badges
  on a product card, the data behind them has other homes — the WhatsApp FAB in
  T-3.10 and Salla's own contact page. The design wins where the information is
  not orphaned.

  WHAT THE DESIGN OMITS AND THIS TEMPLATE KEEPS: the VAT number and the copyright
  hook. A tax disclosure has **no other home in this theme**, and the copyright
  line is injected by the platform through a hook rather than authored here.
  Dropping either to match an artboard would be tidiness at the expense of a
  legal obligation.
#}
<footer data-testid="store-footer" class="store-footer">
    <div class="store-footer__inner container">
        <a href="{{ link('/') }}" class="store-footer__brand">
            <img src="{{ store.logo|cdn(175) }}" alt="{{ store.name }}" width="175" height="40" loading="lazy">
        </a>

        <nav class="store-footer__links" aria-labelledby="footer-links-heading">
            <h2 class="store-footer__heading" id="footer-links-heading">{{ trans('blocks.footer.pages_links') }}</h2>
            <salla-menu data-testid="store-footer-menu" source="footer" with-cookie-preferences></salla-menu>
        </nav>

        <hr class="store-footer__rule">

        {# `salla-social` labels its own links and reflects only the networks the
           merchant configured — so the row is six pills or two, without the theme
           deciding which. Styled from outside; the component is not replaced. #}
        <salla-social data-testid="store-footer-social" class="store-footer__social"></salla-social>

        {# Maroof and the rest come from the platform. B9: the theme never ships a
           third-party trust or payment mark as a bundled image. #}
        <salla-trust-badges data-testid="store-footer-trust-badges"
                            class="store-footer__badges"
                            {% if theme.settings.get('footer_is_dark') %}dark{% endif %}></salla-trust-badges>

        <salla-payments data-testid="store-footer-payments" class="store-footer__payments"></salla-payments>

        {% if store.settings.tax.number %}
            <div class="store-footer__tax">
                <span>{{ trans('common.elements.tax_number') }}</span>
                <b class="bidi-ltr">{{ store.settings.tax.number }}</b>

                {% if store.settings.tax.certificate %}
                    <a class="load-img-onclick" data-modal-id="modal-value-tax" href="#/">
                        <img width="40" height="50" src="{{ 'images/tax.png'|cdn(70,70) }}" loading="lazy"
                             alt="{{ trans('common.elements.tax_number') }}">
                    </a>
                {% endif %}
            </div>

            {% if store.settings.tax.certificate %}
                <salla-modal data-testid="store-footer-tax-modal"
                             sub-title-first
                             sub-title="{{ trans('common.elements.tax_number') }}"
                             modal-title="{{ store.settings.tax.number }}"
                             id="modal-value-tax">
                    <div class="flex justify-center max-w-full">
                        <img class="w-full" loading="lazy"
                             data-src="{{ store.settings.tax.certificate }}"
                             alt="{{ store.settings.tax.number }}">
                    </div>
                </salla-modal>
            {% endif %}
        {% endif %}

        <p class="store-footer__copyright copyright-text">{% hook copyright %}</p>
    </div>
</footer>
